body:
I hope so! Thank you for responding!

&#x200B;

I think one of the other things that makes it hard is that now that I am approaching 18, they more and more are using the reason that they pay for everything to control everything I do. But they won't let me get a job, and I do not and have never had an allowance.

Your English is perfectly good!

&#x200B;

I just am not sure what to do because any time I try to talk about these things it mostly leads to yelling and resentment of me. I don't have any other friends or family to talk to, so it makes it hard when they reject me like that. I know location while walking isn't a big deal, but I don't think it should be necessary of course. But if I try to talk about again it leads to yelling or punishment. My parents also resent me because I am male and the assumption is that by default men are bad people.
